WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:14.119
Mowgli followed the woman into her hut.

2
00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:17.881
He felt nervous, but the woman seemed kind.

3
00:00:18.941 --> 00:00:20.522
Inside the hut was a bed.

4
00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:25.745
He also saw a large chest for storing grain and copper cooking pots.

5
00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:30.968
Hanging on the wall were images of gods and a tall glass.

6
00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:35.934
When Mowgli stepped in front of the glass, he gasped.

7
00:00:35.954 --> 00:00:39.055
"Another boy lives here!"

8
00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:40.656
he thought in surprise.

9
00:00:41.896 --> 00:00:42.977
He lifted an arm.

10
00:00:44.157 --> 00:00:45.698
So did the boy in the glass.

11
00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:48.179
Mowgli wiggled his fingers.

12
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.401
Again the boy did just what Mowgli was doing.

13
00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:55.382
The woman laughed.

14
00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.444
She pointed from Mowgli to the mirror.

15
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.861
"Oh!" Finally Mowgli understood.

16
00:01:03.881 --> 00:01:06.743
"That's me in the glass!"

17
00:01:08.984 --> 00:01:11.305
The woman gave him some milk and bread.

18
00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:14.887
Then she lay her hand on his head.

19
00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:19.789
"Nathoo? Do you remember the shoes I gave you?"

20
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.172
Mowgli shook his head, unable to understand.

21
00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:26.713
The woman touched his foot.

22
00:01:27.794 --> 00:01:29.995
It felt as hard as an animal horn.

23
00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:33.197
"No," she said sadly.

24
00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:36.379
"These feet have never worn shoes.

25
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.423
But you look like my Nathoo, and you shall be my son."

26
00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:46.346
Mowgli had never been under a roof before.

27
00:01:47.587 --> 00:01:51.029
He climbed on a stool to touch the straw over his head.

28
00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:56.093
The hut had a door and a window.

29
00:01:57.114 --> 00:02:00.356
But he could also rip the roof's straw if he felt trapped.

30
00:02:01.296 --> 00:02:02.837
That thought eased his mind.

31
00:02:03.938 --> 00:02:05.759
But something else was bothering him.

32
00:02:05.779 --> 00:02:10.241
"I must learn the humans' language," he realized.

33
00:02:10.261 --> 00:02:14.904
"I cannot live with people if I don't understand their words."

34
00:02:16.745 --> 00:02:20.727
So as soon as Messua pronounced a word, Mowgli repeated it.

35
00:02:22.268 --> 00:02:26.330
Before dark he had learned the names of many things in the hut.

36
00:02:28.431 --> 00:02:32.409
At bedtime Messua and her husband shut the door to the hut.

37
00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.370
Mowgli felt trapped.

38
00:02:42.132 --> 00:02:43.972
He quickly slipped through a window.

39
00:02:43.992 --> 00:02:48.013
"I must fetch him!"

40
00:02:48.393 --> 00:02:49.154
Messua said.

41
00:02:50.474 --> 00:02:51.674
Her husband stopped her.

42
00:02:51.694 --> 00:02:54.435
"Leave him alone," he said.

43
00:02:54.455 --> 00:02:57.716
"The boy has never slept on a bed before.

44
00:02:58.228 --> 00:03:01.109
If he is indeed our son, he won't run away."

45
00:03:04.511 --> 00:03:08.252
Mowgli stretched out in some long grass at the edge of the field.

46
00:03:11.994 --> 00:03:16.956
Before he could close his eyes, a soft gray nose poked him.

47
00:03:20.577 --> 00:03:23.198
Brother!" Mowgli cried in delight.

48
00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:25.919
The wolf sniffed Mowgli.

49
00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.616
"Yuck!" he said.

50
00:03:28.636 --> 00:03:32.117
"This is a terrible reward for following you.

51
00:03:32.957 --> 00:03:37.139
You smell like wood smoke and cattle—human smells!"

52
00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:39.359
Mowgli laughed.

53
00:03:39.979 --> 00:03:43.000
"Is everything okay?"

54
00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.761
"Not exactly," Gray Brother replied.

55
00:03:47.781 --> 00:03:50.502
"I have news about Shere Khan.

56
00:03:51.723 --> 00:03:53.483
He's gone off to hunt for a while.

57
00:03:54.363 --> 00:03:56.664
But the red flower burned him badly.

58
00:03:57.568 --> 00:04:00.349
He promises to hunt you down when he returns.

59
00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:03.910
He wants to lay your bones in the river!"

60
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.871
"He doesn't scare me," Mowgli said.

61
00:04:07.891 --> 00:04:11.552
"I'm going to hunt him down one day!

62
00:04:12.372 --> 00:04:14.533
Even Mother Wolf says that's true."

63
00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.633
Gray Brother looked worried.

64
00:04:17.653 --> 00:04:21.414
"Shere Khan is very dangerous, Mowgli.

65
00:04:21.815 --> 00:04:22.515
Be careful."

66
00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:25.035
"I'll be careful."

67
00:04:25.976 --> 00:04:26.876
Mowgli yawned.

68
00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.922
"I'm so tired tonight.

69
00:04:31.642 --> 00:04:33.803
I learned many new things today.

70
00:04:34.684 --> 00:04:36.725
Please bring me more news soon."

71
00:04:39.347 --> 00:04:41.028
His eyes closed for a moment.

72
00:04:42.368 --> 00:04:44.710
"You won't forget that you're a wolf, will you?"

73
00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.911
Gray Brother asked anxiously.

74
00:04:46.931 --> 00:04:50.133
"Never," Mowgli promised.

75
00:04:50.153 --> 00:04:54.816
"I will always remember that I love you and our cave.

76
00:04:55.808 --> 00:04:58.170
But you must remember something, Gray Brother.

77
00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.292
The wolf pack cast me out."

78
00:05:01.312 --> 00:05:06.536
"The man pack could cast you out too," Gray Brother said.

79
00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:09.718
"People are only people, Mowgli.

80
00:05:10.559 --> 00:05:13.561
Their talk is like the talk of frogs in a pond.

81
00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:14.962
It doesn't mean much."

82
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:17.504
Mowgli shrugged.

83
00:05:17.964 --> 00:05:19.265
His eyes closed again.

84
00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:23.528
"I will let you sleep," Gray Brother said finally.

85
00:05:24.892 --> 00:05:26.474
"I'll come again in a few weeks.

86
00:05:26.975 --> 00:05:28.396
Look for me in the bamboo.

87
00:05:29.237 --> 00:05:31.460
It's at the edge of the people's fields."

88
00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:35.444
"Okay," Mowgli whispered.

89
00:05:35.464 --> 00:05:36.986
"Good night."
